    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-131340",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3ad4e453-00da-5c77-8d6a-5de4dc3d5593",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Curl of a Vector Field",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F={x}^{2}\\,i+xz\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(-2,-3,1).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2} & xz & {z}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-x)i-(0-0)j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,-3,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-2,-3,1) & =-(-2)\\,i+(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\,i-2\\,k"
