    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-131341",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3ad4e453-00da-5c77-8d6a-5de4dc3d5593",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Curl of a Vector Field",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F=(2xy+2z)\\,i+({y}^{2}+1)\\,j+(x+y)\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(-3,0,-1).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 2xy+2z & {y}^{2}+1 & x+y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}+1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xy+2z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+2z)]k \\\\  & =(1-0)i-(1-2)j+(0-2x)k \\\\  & =\\,i+j-2x\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-3,0,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-3,0,-1) & =i+\\,j-2(-3)\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+\\,j+6\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
