      "problem": "Given that $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i+{e}^{xy}\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
